  "spec": "specs.md \u00a721.1, \u00a724, \u00a725",
  "description": "The form takes a whole count of K, M or G, at most 99999, which the plugin reads as powers of 1024. A size is written in the largest of them that holds it exactly; otherwise it is rounded up, in the smallest that holds the count, with the warning minfreespace-rounded: 5% of 1,000,000 bytes, 50,000, is 49K; 5% of 4 TB, 200,000,000,000, exactly 195,312,500K, is 187G. 1536 MiB is 1536M. A size past 99999G is refused with exit 1 and nothing on standard output, as the form cannot hold it; the line of mergerfs still has it.",
